-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",403,{
[12865]="70065B6B\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Dindal's Overlook (total: 12)\tReniaril has asked you to defeat any Orcs you find along the path to Dindal's Overlook. Dindal's Overlook can be found east of Imloth Melui.\n2\tTalk to Reniaril\tYou should inform Reniaril that Dindal's Overlook has been cleared of remnant Orcs. Reniaril can be found south of Imloth Melui and north-east of Arnach.\n",
[12866]="7004DA4A\n1\tDestroy Jangovar banners (total: 12)\030Destroy siege engines (total: 8)\tSiege engines and banners can be found in the encampment of Urûshoba. You should destroy siege engines and banners.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many siege engines and banners.\n",
[12867]="7003468A\n1\tOter asked you to call him over to you on your way to Cuthbald's Farm. On the road south of Thrymm's Farm is likely a good spot to summon him.\t\n2\tTalk to Oter\tNow that he is with you, speak to Oter before heading to Cuthbald's Farm.\n3\tFind Cuthbald's Farm\tCuthbald's Farm is south-east of Thrymm's Farm.\n4\tFind and help Oter's brother\tOter's brother must be on or around Cuthbald's Farm somewhere. With Wargs and Warg-riders around he likely didn't make it far.\n5\tSpeak with Ragnold\tOter's brother was trapped under debris, but appears to be all right. He looks eager to leave Cuthbald's Farm quickly, but would like to speak to you first.\n6\tOter's brother, Ragnold, has gone back to Thrymm's Farm. You should speak to Oter about saving his brother.\t\n7\tSpeak with Oter at Thrymm's Farm\tSince his brother has been saved and has safely returned to Thrymm's Farm, Oter will be eager to speak with you there.\n",
[12868]="7006AE94\n1\tDefeat Wights near Ghâr Mejet (total: 15)\tDangerous foul creatures fill this forsaken area. Seek out these creatures and destroy them before they can harm others.\n2\tTalk to Yâshri outside of Ghâr Mejet\tTalk to Yâshri and let her know that fewer of these creatures haunt this place.\n",
[12869]="700332A6\n1\tSearch an Orc from the Crack's Edge (quantity: see journal)\tOrcs can be found surrounding the Crack's Edge in Nud-melek, near the sundered Bridge of Khazad-dûm. You should interrogate Orcs to find out what happened at the Bridge of Khazad-dûm to cause such restlessness.\n2\tBring the charred papers to Svanr\tSvanr can be found at the shattered Bridge of Khazad-dûm on the west edge of the chasm in Nud-melek. You should speak with Svanr.\n",
[12870]="70046BE2\n1\tTalk to Duinhir near Cair Andros\tYou should talk to Duinhir, who can be found near Cair Andros in North Ithilien.\n2\tTalk to Duinhir near Cair Andros\tYou should talk to Duinhir, who can be found near Cair Andros.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn at the Host of the West encampment\tAragorn can be found at the Host of the West encampment, on the border of North Ithilien and Dagorlad. You should Talk to Aragorn.\n",
[12871]="7005466F\n1\tComplete Instance: Ambush at Echad Taerdim\tLegolas wishes to return to Echad Taerdim with an injured Atli Spider-bane. You should speak with Legolas near Taurlingol to begin the journey.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas has returned to Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should talk to Legolas.\n3\tTalk to Felgúr\tFelgúr has been taken prisoner, and is being kept in Echad Taerdim. You should talk to Felgúr.\n4\tTalk to Mablung\tFelgúr has asked you to propose a deal to Mablung on his behalf. You should talk to Mablung in Echad Taerdim.\n5\tTalk to Atli\tAtli Spider-bane is resting at Echad Taerdim. You should see how Atli is faring after Rûkhor's assault.\n6\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[12872]="7004C030\n1\tComplete: The Bloody Watchers\t\n2\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron is waiting for you at the Agarnaith Ranger camp. You should talk to Faeron.\n3\tFind the Rangers in Seregost\tFaeron and Rhadrog are somewhere inside Seregost. You should find the Rangers.\n4\tTalk to Faeron\030Talk to Rhadrog\tFaeron is outside the Court of Seregost, in Agarnaith. You should talk to Faeron.\n5\tComplete: The Court of Seregost\030Complete: The Court of Seregost - Tier 2\tComplete: The Court of Seregost.\n6\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found at the Agarnaith Ranger camp. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[12873]="7004E3DF\n1\tDefeat Thrâng\tYou have found yourself in Thrâng's arena. You should defeat Thrâng!\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[12874]="7006025B\n1\tReach the top of Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire, can be found at Agal Dûn. You should reach the top of Tûr Fúar.\n2\tTalk to Brathar Crack-helm at the top of Tûr Fúar\030Talk to Rethvárd at the top of Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire, can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Brathar Crack-helm and Rethvárd at the top of Tûr Fúar.\n3\tTalk to Múta at the top of Tûr Fúar\030Talk to Mézto at the top of Tûr Fúar\030Talk to Prince Ingór at the top of Tûr Fúar\030Talk to Glóin at the top of Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Múta, Mézto, Prince Ingór, and Glóin at the top of Tûr Fúar.\n4\tTalk to Domongart at the top of Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Domongart, Chieftain of the Trév Duvárdain, at the top of Tûr Fúar.\n5\tTalk to Hraubrek at the top of Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire, can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Hraubrek, Chieftain of the Grímklettar, at the top of Tûr Fúar.\n",
[12875]="70046C3C\n1\tTalk to Jarl Gurthilm\tJarl Gurthilm can be found across the river to the south-west of Uya Hujûm. You have rallied to Jarl Gurthilm's side and should now aid him and his company in seeking vengeance against the Khundolar.\n2\tTalk to Jarl Gurthilm in the southern reaches of Dagorlad\tJarl Gurthilm can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad. You have defeated the Khundolar and their treacherous leader and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm.\n",
[12876]="700001FB\n1\tTalk to Lindir\tLindir is with Bilbo in the Hall of Fire at Rivendell. Bilbo told you that Lindir has a new riddle to offer, one out of Gondor.\n2\tFind the answer to Lindir's riddle somewhere in Rivendell\tThe answer to Lindir's riddle can be found somewhere in Rivendell. Lindir has asked you to find an item that provides an answer to his riddle. Breath is needed Warning heeded Some will arrive With sword and knife My work is completed 'Til once more I am needed.\n3\tBring Boromir's badge to Lindir\tLindir is with Bilbo in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House. Boromir has given you a token that provides the answer to Lindir's riddle and told you to bring it to Lindir.\n",
[12877]="700001FC\n1\tTalk to Lindir\tLindir is standing with Bilbo in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House. Bilbo has asked you to speak with Lindir about the riddle he presented to the old hobbit.\n2\tBring the gloves to Lindir at the Last Homely House\030Find an item that solves Lindir's riddle\tThe answer to Lindir's riddle lies somewhere in the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Lindir awaits your return in the Hall of Fire. Lindir is waiting for you to bring him the answer to his riddle.\n",
[12878]="700001FD\n1\tTalk to Bilbo\tBilbo is standing with Lindir in the Hall of Fire. Lindir told you that it was Bilbo's turn to present a riddle and that you should speak with him.\n2\tBring the besom broom to Bilbo Baggins in the Hall of Fire\030Find an item that solves Bilbo's riddle\tThe solution to Bilbo's riddle is somewhere in the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Bilbo awaits your return in the Hall of Fire. Bilbo is waiting for you to bring him the item that solves his riddle.\n",
[12879]="700001E9\n1\tBring Celebrían's legacy to Glorfindel\030Collect Celebrían's legacy\tThe lost Elf-vault is somewhere in the Trollshaws in the vicinity of Rivendell, probably on the High Moor. Glorfindel awaits your return outside the house of Elrond, by the waterfall. Glorfindel told you to seek the vault on the High Moor and advised you to place a hand upon a rock beside the entrance of the Elf-vault and to recite the verses of the riddle. Celebrían's legacy for Arwen, a white jewel, should be somewhere within the vault.\n2\tDeliver Celebrían's legacy to Elrond\tElrond is in the library of Rivendell. Glorfindel asked you to bring Arwen's legacy to Elrond.\n",
[12880]="700001EA\n1\tTalk to Bilbo\tBilbo is standing with Lindir in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House. Lindir told you to speak with Bilbo to learn the unsolved riddle.\n2\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is in his library in the Last Homely House. Bilbo believes Elrond may know more about the riddle. The jewel of the moon, Enshrined in the water, From mother to daughter Is given a boon. Ships sail to the west, Forgetting all sorrow, Landfall on the morrow, The isles of the blest.\n3\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel is outside the house of Elrond, by the waterfall. Elrond has directed you to speak to Glorfindel about the riddle. The jewel of the moon, Enshrined in the water, From mother to daughter Is given a boon. Ships sail to the west, Forgetting all sorrow, Landfall on the morrow, The isles of the blest.\n",
[12881]="700173C8\n1\tDefeat Glothrok the Vile\030Defeat Forzunk\tGlothrok the Vile is within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch. Thithrand seemed unnerved at the sight of a powerful goblin riding an even more powerful-looking Warg. The pair entered the Grand Stair at the head of the Warg-riders and have not been seen since.\n2\tTalk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch\tThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Thithrand with news of your victory.\n",
[12882]="700453E0\n1\tHike to the top of Amon Dîn\tAmon Dîn is located in eastern Taur Drúadan. You should climb atop Amon Dîn and meet with Bregdal.\n2\tSpeak with Bregdal atop Amon Dîn\tBregdal is atop Amon Dîn. You should speak with Bregdal.\n3\tDefeat Mordor Orcs in Taur Drúadan (total: 6)\tMordor Orcs can be found throughout Taur Drúadan. You should defeat Mordor Orcs to allow Bregdal safe passage to the Rohirrim encampment.\n4\tSpeak with Bregdal at the War-stead of the King's Men\tBregdal is at the War-stead of the King's Men, near Eilenach. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[12883]="7002EFA6\n1\tSpeak with Burnoth to learn more about his men and their mission\tBurnoth is at the refugee-camp outside Harwick in the Wold. You should speak with Burnoth if you would know more of his men and their mission.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth at the refugee-camp outside Harwick\tBurnoth is at the refugee-camp outside of Harwick in the Wold. You should speak again with Burnoth.\n",
[12884]="700455DE\n1\tDestroy caltrops on the road outside of Ost Rimmon (total: 8)\tCaltrops can be found on and around the road outside of Ost Rimmon. Variags have laid traps along the road to slow the forces of Rohan. You should disarm these traps before any more horses are wounded.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth in Ost Rimmon\tBurnoth can be found within Ost Rimmon in the Beacon Hills. You have destroyed the caltrops and should now return to Burnoth.\n3\tCollect sets of horseshoes (total: 3)\tSets of horseshoes can be found within Ost Rimmon in the Beacon Hills. Burnoth has asked you to aid him in shoeing the horses before he and his fellows set off.\n4\tShoe Brynmód\030Shoe Flyting\030Shoe Gesith\tThe steeds of the Riders Three can be found at the stables of Ost Rimmon. You have collected enough horseshoes and should now shoe the steeds of the Riders Three.\n5\tTalk to Hutha\tHutha is at Ost Rimmon. You have shoed the steeds and should now speak to Hutha as Burnoth asked.\n6\tTalk to Ulf\tUlf is at Ost Rimmon. You have spoken to Hutha and should now speak to Ulf as well.\n",
[12885]="7002BD51\n1\tDefeat Penrith\tAndras asked you to enter Saruman's Foundry and defeat his acolyte, Penrith, a Dunlending who has forsaken the ways of the clans and has embraced the world of the foul magic called 'industry' which Saruman espouses.\n",
[12886]="7002BD4F\n1\tTake Saruman's rings and destroy them\tAndras has asked you to enter the tower of Orthanc and wrest Saruman's rings from him and dispose of them before the curse of the Nazgûl can fall upon any of his people.\n",
[12887]="7006AB5F\n1\tDefeat crypt-walkers (total: 6)\030Defeat crypt-sentries (total: 5)\030Defeat crypt-bellowers (total: 3)\tKhôltekh has asked you to venture into Sektakhâb and cull the rising population of the Dead. You can find them west of Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir guard outpost in southern Khabârkhad.\n2\tReturn to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.\n",
[12888]="7000D3C8\n1\tTalk to Osbail\030Talk to Camran\030Talk to Tasgall\tOsbail is by Crannog's ruling-seat in Aughaire, Camran is at the centre island of the settlement, and Tasgall is still hunting hill-beasts north of Aughaire and south-east of Nád Nathair. Crannog has advised you to speak with the people of Aughaire to learn what you may about your upcoming challenge: the Clúcath with the Trév Duvárdain.\n2\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog is at his ruling-seat in Aughaire, west of the settlement's central island. You have spoken with some of the Trév Gállorg and should return to Crannog as he advised.\n3\tTalk to Crannog and travel to Fail-á-Khro\tCrannog is at his ruling-seat in Aughaire, west of the settlement's central island. Crannog is waiting for you to speak with him so you may travel together to Fail-á-Khro for the Clúcath with the Trév Duvárdain.\n4\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog is at his ruling-seat in Aughaire, west of the settlement's central island. You have emerged victorious from the Clúcath with the Trév Duvárdain and should now speak with Crannog.\n",
[12889]="700529DF\n1\tCollect Anduin moss (total: 10)\030Collect river reeds (total: 10)\tAnduin moss and river reeds can be gathered from the river-banks of the Anduin in Duskenvale. You should collect Anduin moss and river reeds.\n2\tTalk to Ingelfled\tIngelfled can be found in the village of Arhaim in Duskenvale. You should deliver the moss and reeds to Ingelfled.\n",
[12890]="7002EEEF\n1\tSpeak to a guard at the second southernmost watch-tower\tThe second southernmost watch-tower can be found on the edge of the Great River in the northern Wold, south-east of Langhold. You should ride to the watch-tower and ensure that all is well.\n2\tSpeak to a guard at the central watch-tower\tThe central watch-tower can be found on the edge of the Great River in the northern Wold, slightly north of the first tower. You should ride to the watch-tower and ensure that all is well.\n3\tSpeak to a watchman at the northern central tower\tThe highest watch-tower can be found on the tallest hill overlooking the Great River in the northern Wold, slightly north of the first tower. You should ride to the watch-tower and ensure that all is well.\n4\tSpeak to the watchman guarding the northernmost tower\tThe watch-tower at the Great River's edge can be found north of the high tower, down the slopes towards the water. You should speak with the watchman at the river-edge tower.\n",
[12891]="70071CC9\n1\tDefeat zizani near Charganpâta (total: 12)\tThe fisher Kôrzan has requested you deal with the nearby zizani, who have moved into the best fishing spots along the White-wrath river. The zizani can be found clustered near the foetid ponds of Charganpâta. Charganpâta is north-east of Sen Chatâk.\n2\tReturn to Kôrzan in Sen Chatâk\tReturn to Kôrzan in Sen Chatâk with news of your success.\n",
[12892]="7002609E\n1\tTalk to Albin Northcotton\tAlbin Northcotton is at the Northcotton Farm. Albin Northcotton will be pleased to hear that Nibs is ready and the road is clear.\n",
[12893]="7002D3F1\n1\tPlant a banner to claim the Lonely Span for the dwarves\tThe Lonely Span can be found by following the east path past the Cooling Chamber from the Dolven-view camp. You should head to the Lonely Span and plant a banner of the dwarves there.\n2\tReturn to Sót at the Dolven-view\tSót is in the Dolven-view in the Great Delving of Moria. You should return to Sót now that the bridge to the Twenty-first Hall has been claimed by the dwarf-expedition.\n",
[12894]="7007177E\n1\tGo to the cross-roads in An Shêru\tKhagâmi would like to meet you near a road crossing to the west in An Shêru to rest for the night.\n2\tTalk to Khagâmi\tYou have met Khagâmi at the site near a road crossing in An Shêru she told you about. You should talk to her.\n",
[12895]="7003A2B0\n1\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. You must complete the quests 'Edoras: In Need of Cheering-up', 'Book 12, Chapter 5: Eyes of Edoras', and 'Book 12, Chapter 6: Through the Net' before Éowyn's people can depart for Dunharrow.\t\n2\tTalk to Éowyn outside Meduseld\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. You have finished readying Éowyn and her people. You should now speak to Éowyn.\n3\tTalk to Éowyn\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. You have prepared the people of Middlemead and the Harrowdale for their journey to Dunharrow. You should now speak to Éowyn.\n4\tTalk to Éowyn at Dunharrow\tÉowyn can be found with the people of Kingstead on the Firienfeld at Dunharrow. You have defended the people of Rohan as they made shelter. You should speak to Éowyn.\n",
[12896]="7001E4BB\n1\tTalk to Fuirgam in Emyn Lum\tFuirgam should be among the Malledhrim at their stronghold in Emyn Lûm. You should seek Fuirgam and establish a line of communication between the Elves of Emyn Lûm and the Dourstocks.\n",
})
